IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc6-builders`

-- ccc6-s153-1.l4 -- s 153.1, Sexual exploitation of person with disability: the offence, its punishment, the definition of consent, when no consent is obtained,
-- the bar on a belief in consent, and the judge's duty to instruct the jury.
-- The offence function takes the complainant's consent as the answer of `s 153.1(2) consent` (JUST FALSE is "without that person's consent").

§ `s 153.1 Sexual exploitation of person with disability`

-- (3) is encoded first because (2) and (1) read it. The list is open ("Nothing in subsection (3) shall be construed as limiting the circumstances", subsection (4)):
-- a case none of (a) to (e) covers is NOTHING, not "consent was obtained".
-- src:3068 | When no consent obtained
-- src:3069 | (3) For the purposes of this section, no consent is obtained if
-- src:3070 | (a) the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant;
-- src:3071 | (a.1) the complainant is unconscious;
-- src:3072 | (b) the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for any reason other than the one referred to in paragraph (a.1);
-- src:3073 | (c) the accused counsels or incites the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority;
-- src:3074 | (d) the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity; or
-- src:3075 | (e) the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(3) (src:3068-3075)
GIVEN `the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant is unconscious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for a reason other than being unconscious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused counsels or incites the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153.1(3) no consent is obtained` MEANS
    IF    `the agreement is expressed by the words or conduct of a person other than the complainant`
       OR `the complainant is unconscious`
       OR `the complainant is incapable of consenting to the activity for a reason other than being unconscious`
       OR `the accused counsels or incites the complainant to engage in the activity by abusing a position of trust, power or authority`
       OR `the complainant expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to engage in the activity`
       OR `the complainant, having consented to engage in sexual activity, expresses, by words or conduct, a lack of agreement to continue to engage in the activity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Nothing in subsection (3) shall be construed as limiting the circumstances in which no consent is obtained"

-- src:3076 | Subsection (3) not limiting
-- src:3077 | (4) Nothing in subsection (3) shall be construed as limiting the circumstances in which no consent is obtained.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(4) (src:3076-3077)
`s 153.1(4) subsection (3) limits the circumstances in which no consent is obtained` MEANS
    JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in subsection (3) shall be construed as limiting the circumstances in which no consent is obtained"

-- src:3066 | Question of law
-- src:3067 | (2.2) The question of whether no consent is obtained under subsection (3) or (4) or 265(3) is a question of law.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(2.2) (src:3066-3067)
GIVEN `the question is whether no consent is obtained under subsection (3) or (4) or 265(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153.1(2.2) the question is a question of law` MEANS
    IF `the question is whether no consent is obtained under subsection (3) or (4) or 265(3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The question of whether no consent is obtained under subsection (3) or (4) or 265(3) is a question of law"

-- (2) "Subject to subsection (3), consent means, for the purposes of this section, the voluntary agreement of the complainant to engage in the sexual activity in question." (2.1) "Consent must be present at the time the sexual activity in question takes place."
-- Subsection (3) is open (subsection (4)), so the function also takes "another circumstance in which no consent is obtained" (for example one of s 265(3)) as a plain fact.
-- src:3062 | Definition of consent
-- src:3063 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), consent means, for the purposes of this section, the voluntary agreement of the complainant to engage in the sexual activity in question.
-- src:3064 | Consent
-- src:3065 | (2.1) Consent must be present at the time the sexual activity in question takes place.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(2) (src:3062-3065)
GIVEN `the complainant voluntarily agreed to engage in the sexual activity in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement was present at the time the sexual activity in question took place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 153.1(3) no consent is obtained` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `another circumstance, outside subsection (3), in which no consent is obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153.1(2) consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 153.1(3) no consent is obtained` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `another circumstance, outside subsection (3), in which no consent is obtained`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to subsection (3), consent means, for the purposes of this section, the voluntary agreement of the complainant"
        IF NOT `the complainant voluntarily agreed to engage in the sexual activity in question`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "consent means, for the purposes of this section, the voluntary agreement of the complainant to engage in the sexual activity in question"
        IF NOT `the agreement was present at the time the sexual activity in question took place`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Consent must be present at the time the sexual activity in question takes place"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 153.1(1) what the person counselled or incited the other person to do` IS ONE OF
    `s 153.1(1)(a) touch their own body, the body of the person who so counsels or incites or the body of any other person, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object`
    `s 153.1(1)(b) expose their own sexual organs`
    `s 153.1(1) something else`

-- src:3054 | Sexual exploitation of person with disability
-- src:3055 | 153.1 (1) Every person commits an offence who is in a position of trust or authority towards a person with a mental or physical disability or who is a person with whom a person with a mental or physical disability is in a relationship of dependency and who, for a sexual purpose, counsels or incites that person to, without that person’s consent,
-- src:3056 | (a) touch their own body, the body of the person who so counsels or incites or the body of any other person, directly or indirectly, with a part of the body or with an object; or
-- src:3057 | (b) expose their own sexual organs.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(1) (src:3054-3057)
GIVEN `the person is in a position of trust or authority towards a person with a mental or physical disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person with whom a person with a mental or physical disability is in a relationship of dependency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person counselled or incited the person with the disability for a sexual purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `what the person counselled or incited the person with the disability to do` IS A `s 153.1(1) what the person counselled or incited the other person to do`
      `s 153.1(2) consent` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153.1(1) the conduct is the offence of sexual exploitation of a person with a disability` MEANS
    IF    (   `the person is in a position of trust or authority towards a person with a mental or physical disability`
           OR `the person is a person with whom a person with a mental or physical disability is in a relationship of dependency`)
      AND `the person counselled or incited the person with the disability for a sexual purpose`
      AND NOT (`what the person counselled or incited the person with the disability to do` EQUALS `s 153.1(1) something else`)
      AND `s 153.1(2) consent` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every person commits an offence who is in a position of trust or authority towards a person with a mental or physical disability or who is a person with whom a person with a mental or physical disability is in a relationship of dependency and who, for a sexual purpose, counsels or incites that person to, without that person’s consent"

-- src:3058 | Punishment
-- src:3059 | (1.1) Every person who commits an offence under subsection (1) is guilty of
-- src:3060 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 10 years; or
-- src:3061 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(1.1) (src:3058-3061)
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 153.1(1.1)(a) the punishment on indictment` MEANS
    Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- (b) "an offence punishable on summary conviction": no penalty is stated here; the penalty is that of s 787(1), taken as an input (another part).
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(1.1)(b) (src:3061)
GIVEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 153.1(1.1)(b) the punishment on summary conviction` MEANS
    `ss 150 to 182 the punishment on summary conviction that s 787(1) fixes` `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(1.1) (src:3058-3061)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 153.1 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- (5) "It is not a defence to a charge under this section that the accused believed that the complainant consented ... if (a), (b) or (c)": the bar applies (JUST TRUE) when one of the three holds.
-- src:3078 | When belief in consent not a defence
-- src:3079 | (5) It is not a defence to a charge under this section that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge if
-- src:3080 | (a) the accused’s belief arose from
-- src:3081 | (i) the accused’s self-induced intoxication,
-- src:3082 | (ii) the accused’s recklessness or wilful blindness, or
-- src:3083 | (iii) any circumstance referred to in subsection (3) or (4) or 265(3) in which no consent is obtained;
-- src:3084 | (b) the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting; or
-- src:3085 | (c) there is no evidence that the complainant’s voluntary agreement to the activity was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(5) (src:3078-3085)
GIVEN `the accused is charged under section 153.1 and alleges that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused's belief arose from the accused's self-induced intoxication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused's belief arose from the accused's recklessness or wilful blindness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused's belief arose from a circumstance referred to in subsection (3) or (4) or 265(3) in which no consent is obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is no evidence that the complainant's voluntary agreement to the activity was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153.1(5) the belief that the complainant consented is not a defence: the bar applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is charged under section 153.1 and alleges that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not a defence to a charge under this section that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the activity that forms the subject-matter of the charge"
        IF    `the accused's belief arose from the accused's self-induced intoxication`
           OR `the accused's belief arose from the accused's recklessness or wilful blindness`
           OR `the accused's belief arose from a circumstance referred to in subsection (3) or (4) or 265(3) in which no consent is obtained`
           OR `the accused did not take reasonable steps, in the circumstances known to the accused at the time, to ascertain that the complainant was consenting`
           OR `there is no evidence that the complainant's voluntary agreement to the activity was affirmatively expressed by words or actively expressed by conduct`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is not a defence ... if (a) the accused’s belief arose from ... (b) the accused did not take reasonable steps ... or (c) there is no evidence"

-- (6) the judge "shall instruct the jury": a duty on the judge, with its conditions. It is a duty, so a failed "if" is JUST FALSE (the provision's own question; fork F6).
-- The duty is also written as a regulative rule below (PARTY a judge MUST ...); a DEONTIC value cannot be asserted on the stable binary (finding in NOTES.md), so the decision function carries the assertions.
-- src:3086 | Accused’s belief as to consent
-- src:3087 | (6) If an accused alleges that he or she believed that the complainant consented to the conduct that is the subject-matter of the charge, a judge, if satisfied that there is sufficient evidence and that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence, shall instruct the jury, when reviewing all the evidence relating to the determination of the honesty of the accused’s belief, to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for that belief.
@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(6) (src:3086-3087)
GIVEN `the accused alleges that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the conduct that is the subject-matter of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge is satisfied that there is sufficient evidence and that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 153.1(6) the judge must instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief` MEANS
    IF    `the accused alleges that the accused believed that the complainant consented to the conduct that is the subject-matter of the charge`
      AND `the judge is satisfied that there is sufficient evidence and that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused alleges that he or she believed that the complainant consented to the conduct that is the subject-matter of the charge, a judge, if satisfied that there is sufficient evidence and that, if believed by the jury, the evidence would constitute a defence, shall instruct the jury"

DECLARE `s 153.1(6) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 153.1(6) instruct the jury, when reviewing the evidence on the honesty of the belief, to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for it`

@ref Criminal Code s 153.1(6) (src:3086-3087)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 153.1(6) act`
`s 153.1(6) the judge's duty to instruct the jury` MEANS
    PARTY `a judge`
    MUST `s 153.1(6) instruct the jury, when reviewing the evidence on the honesty of the belief, to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for it`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a judge` BECAUSE "the judge did not instruct the jury to consider the presence or absence of reasonable grounds for the belief"
